deepin-meshlink (26.4.0.0~alpha1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Version scheme switched to <yy>.<quarter>.<x>.<y>; 26.4.0.0 is the first
    alpha of 2026 Q4.
  * Network: select the LAN segment in the first-start wizard, switch it live
    from Settings; heartbeats are broadcast into and accepted only from the
    selected IPv4 segment (manual bootstrap peers remain honoured).
  * Rooms: 32-hex room fingerprint ids plus a unique six-digit numeric invite
    code; join by invite code from the Discover page (LAN-local lookup).
  * Storage: forward migration rekeys legacy 16-hex room ids to 32-hex and
    backfills invite codes, cascading to members/messages/announcements.
  * Protocol: bump to v2 (heartbeat format + room snapshot invite code).

 -- HuanSoft Open Source Community <yxzl666xx@outlook.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:05:00 +0800

deepin-meshlink (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of the deepin-MeshLink MVP.
  * UC-01/02: local Ed25519 account with 32-hex fingerprint, AES-256-GCM
    encrypted keystore, profile editing and full account destruction.
  * UC-03/04: signed UDP heartbeats, LAN peer discovery, offline pruning,
    farewell packets and spoofed-heartbeat reporting.
  * UC-05/06/07: hosted rooms, open/approval join policies, capacity limits,
    host-admin-member moderation matrix, mute, kick and blacklist.
  * UC-08: TLS 1.3 relayed text and image messages with authoritative
    sequence numbers; image bytes fetched on demand by content hash.
  * UC-09/10/11/12: file announcements, supplier registry, explicit
    request-only chunked downloads, persisted per-chunk resume, parallel
    workers and SHA-256 verification with targeted retransmission.
  * UC-13: leave room and host dissolve notifications.

 -- HuanSoft Open Source Community <yxzl666xx@outlook.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:20:00 +0800
